4.m:
I shall relate in full the account of that Manu Vaivasvata,
for your benefit, if you wish to hear it here;
this great foundation is established in the Purāṇa.

The sages said:
Recite in detail, Lomaharṣaṇa, the birth of Pṛthu,
and how this earth was milked by that great-souled one;

The Earth said:
“I will do all this, O hero, there is no doubt;
but look out a calf for me, through which I, full of love, may flow.

5.m:
Lomaharṣaṇa said:
The details cannot be told in even hundreds of years, O twice-born;
hear about all the manvantaras in brief, O twice-born.

8.m:
Lomaharṣaṇa said:
Sagara had two wives whose sins had been burned by asceticism;
the elder, the daughter of the king of Vidarbha, was named Keśinī.
